371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (In This phase presents the results of the Exploratory Data Analysis \(EDA\) conducted for both primary and secondary datasets related to the Saudi Labor Law. The purpose of this analysis is to better understand the content and structure of various legal and public data sources that reflect different perspectives on labor regulations in Saudi Arabia. The analysis aims to identify key patterns, relationships, and differences across four main data sources: the official labor law from the Board of Experts \(BOE\), public consultation data from the Istitlaa platform, explanatory articles from the Qiwa platform \(Qiwa Articles\), and user-generated questions from the Qiwa FAQ section. These datasets together provide a comprehensive view of how labor law information is presented, interpreted, and discussed across official and public platforms. This EDA was performed after completing the data processing and cleaning phase to ensure the accuracy and reliability of the findings. A combination of descriptive statistics, textual visualizations, and comparative charts was used to uncover meaningful trends and thematic similarities between the datasets. The results of each dataset were analyzed and presented separately to highlight their unique characteristics, potential biases, and target audiences. Finally, the report includes a comparative overview and a summary of the main insights and new hypotheses derived from the analysis.)
/E (In This phase presents the results of the Exploratory Data Analysis \(EDA\) conducted for both primary and secondary datasets related to the Saudi Labor Law. The purpose of this analysis is to better understand the content and structure of various legal and public data sources that reflect different perspectives on labor regulations in Saudi Arabia. The analysis aims to identify key patterns, relationships, and differences across four main data sources: the official labor law from the Board of Experts \(BOE\), public consultation data from the Istitlaa platform, explanatory articles from the Qiwa platform \(Qiwa Articles\), and user-generated questions from the Qiwa FAQ section. These datasets together provide a comprehensive view of how labor law information is presented, interpreted, and discussed across official and public platforms. This EDA was performed after completing the data processing and cleaning phase to ensure the accuracy and reliability of the findings. A combination of descriptive statistics, textual visualizations, and comparative charts was used to uncover meaningful trends and thematic similarities between the datasets. The results of each dataset were analyzed and presented separately to highlight their unique characteristics, potential biases, and target audiences. Finally, the report includes a comparative overview and a summary of the main insights and new hypotheses derived from the analysis.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
